WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.435 line:0%
-"A Very Punchable Face" --

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.537 line:0%
how did you come up
with this title?

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:09.442 line:0%
-Just, like, looking in the
mirror, kind of being honest.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.945 line:0%
-Come on. I --
-I got a lot of --

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:18.484 line:0%
-As a friend and as an elder
statesman, I don't like this.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.587 line:0%
I don't want
anyone punching your face.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.556 line:0%
And if someone did,
I would get your back.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.757 line:0%
-Well, thank you, thank you.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.126
That was also
a real concern of my parents

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.596
when I told them
the idea for a title.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.630
They were very concerned
that it would more of

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.033
an invitation
than a description.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.435
But people --
I've heard it from a lot of --

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:39.706
I've heard it from a lot of
friends that were like --

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.808
Like, in a nice way,
but were kind of like,

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.010
"You look like a little --

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.078
There's some punchable
elements there."

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:50.816 line:0%
-I will say, it's a fast read.
It's a really funny book.

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:53.453 line:0%
If you don't even get to
the reading part,

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.720 line:0%
the chapters are funny.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.622 line:0%
Can I just go through
some of these chapters?

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.090 line:0%
-Please.
-Here's one I liked.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:03.730 line:0%
This chapter is called "Oops, I
Fell Asleep in a Graveyard."

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.665 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.734 line:0%
-Oh, and I love this,
'cause this was

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.603 line:0%
"The Time
Jimmy Buffett Saved My Life."

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.239 line:0%
And then I had a question,
'cause I go, "Wait.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.509 line:0%
Oh, he means --" And then you
put, in parenthesis,

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.945 line:0%
"(And I Don't
Just Mean With his Music)".

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.281 line:0%
So there's a story there.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.651 line:0%
-There's a story of him
saving my life, yes.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.253 line:0%
-Yeah. But I was like,
"Oh, I think what

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.387 line:0%
he's talking about
is something --

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.055 line:0%
He heard a song,
and that changed his life."

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:33.960 line:0%
But he actually -- It's --
These stories are great.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.328 line:0%
You stole a photo from
Bill Murray's house.

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:37.730 line:0%
Can we talk about that
on the show?

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.565 line:0%
I can edit this out
if you want me to.

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.200 line:0%
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.970
I'm so mortified by it
and I kind of --

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.906
I kind of put it in
the book as a confession.

00:01:47.906 --> 00:01:51.610
You know, I believe
Mr. Murray, also Catholic,

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.480
so I hope he understands
the concept of

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.617
confession, penance,
forgiveness.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.320
But I was --
When I was a writer at "SNL,"

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.387
I was at his house.

00:02:02.387 --> 00:02:03.756
It was a Christmas party.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.792
And my friend and I
were walking around, like,

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:10.196
with our -- you know, like,
starry-eyed that we were there.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.598
And we were, like,
wandering the house,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.032
because everyone
was all over the place.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:17.971
And we, at some point, passed,
like, a box of stuff that --

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.139
And it was just like
we looked in the box,

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.574
and there were
all these photos of

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.475
Bill Murray
and Richard Pryor together.

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.944
It's Richard Pryor, like,

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.546
putting Bill Murray
in a headlock.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.147
And it was,
like, such a cool photo.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.848
And there were like 10 of them.

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:32.518
And it truly looked like
he was throwing them away,

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:33.919
I swear to God.

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:37.624
And I was like, "He's not gonna
miss one of the 10

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.525
that he's throwing away, right?"

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.327
And so I was like,
"I got to -- I'll --"

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.096
I was like, "I will --"
It felt like not stealing.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:47.600
It felt like one man's trash
is another man's treasure.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.803
And I think now,
as a person who finds treasure

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:54.273
full time with
a metal detector,

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.776 line:0%
I'm coming from
that perspective now.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.744 line:0%
-I understand.
You know, I take it back.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.813 line:0%
I agree. You're so right.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.781 line:0%
Colin, when we have
our guests on the show,

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:05.384 line:0%
we want to know if there's any
charities or organizations

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.885 line:0%
that they'd like to talk about.

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:10.156 line:0%
And you chose this organization
called REACH.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.190 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.258 line:0%
-Would you like to
talk about that

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.059 line:0%
and just tell me what
that's about?

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:16.295
-Yes, I would love to.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:19.765
So, I went to this --
I got into this high school

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.333
that was in Manhattan.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.702
I grew up on Staten Island,
and there was this school

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.504
I got into called
Regis High School

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.439
that is a free school.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.275
It's a really good
academic school,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.944
and if you get in there,
there's no tuition.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:35.514
They started this program,
REACH, and what it does is --

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:40.086
it is basically a boot camp
from 5th to 8th grade

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.421
for kids who are
economically disadvantaged

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.090
from all of
the boroughs of New York.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.026
And it helps get them
extra training

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.095
and help, intensively,
in the summer

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.863
and also throughout
the school year

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.265
to basically bridge the gap
that exists

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:54.366
for a lot of kids in New York.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:56.035
It's super-effective.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.369
So many of the kids get into

00:03:57.369 --> 00:04:00.405
great high schools, great
colleges, have great careers.

00:04:00.405 --> 00:04:03.075
And it's like -- It's just a --
They do such a good job.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:06.278
And I just -- For me,
education was the way out,

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.548
and I think that's such a great

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:11.150
way up for everyone in New York.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.352 line:0%
-Thanks for doing that and
thanks for talking about that.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:15.054 line:0%
And congrats on the book.
-Thank you.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.789 line:0%
-My man, Colin Jost.
-Thank you.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.958 line:0%
-Oh, my gosh.
This is awesome, buddy.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.060 line:0%
I can't wait to see you in
person, hopefully soon.

